# Working files that are never committed. The reason is the same for
# every entry: git history is permanent, so a file committed once is
# exposed for as long as the repository is, and an ignore pattern costs
# nothing while an unstaged mistake cannot be taken back. What these
# name is local to whoever is working in the tree. None of it is part of
# the product, and nothing that is part of the product is ignored.
memory-mirror/
BRIEF.md
archive/

# Local tool state
.claude/settings.local.json

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/

# OS
.DS_Store
